  "namespaces": [
    {
      "name": "SAFEGUARD",
      "comment": "Security Rule safeguard-to-evidence register (45 CFR 164.308/310/312, HIPAA-001/002). Each entry maps one Security Rule safeguard (from the closed catalog, projected into core.allowed-values) to its implementing evidence — a reused POLICY, an ADR, or a control decision — resolved by core.cross-ref. Path-claim with an `id` so a BAA or an audit can cross-ref a safeguard mapping. hipaa.safeguard-evidence (HIPAA-002) enforces the addressable/required distinction: every in-scope safeguard needs an implementing POLICY/ADR cross-ref, and an addressable one may substitute a `justification` field where a required one may not. The generator emits the Addressable id subset (the `requirement` flag from this extract) as that rule's `addressable` param.",
      "paths": ["docs/compliance/hipaa/safeguards/**"],
      "rules": [
        "core.frontmatter",
        "core.id",
        "core.id-unique",
        "core.cross-ref",
        "core.required-metadata",
        "core.allowed-values",
        "hipaa.safeguard-evidence"
      ],
      "required_metadata": [
        "id",
        "title",
        "status",
        "safeguard"
      ],
      "allowed_values": [
        "safeguard"
      ],
      "safeguard_evidence": {
        "vocabulary": "safeguard"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "BAA",
      "comment": "Business Associate Agreement register (45 CFR 164.308(b)(1) / 164.314, HIPAA-003). Each business associate handling ePHI carries an entry recording the contracting party and the execution date, kept fresh on a yearly review cadence (core.calendar-freshness over reviewed_date) — the same registry shape as GDPR's DPA. Path-claim with an `id` so a SAFEGUARD business-associate-contracts safeguard can cross-ref its governing agreement.",
      "paths": ["docs/compliance/hipaa/baa/**"],
      "rules": [
        "core.frontmatter",
        "core.id",
        "core.id-unique",
        "core.cross-ref",
        "core.required-metadata",
        "core.calendar-freshness"
      ],
      "required_metadata": [
        "id",
        "title",
        "status",
        "party",
        "executed_date",
        "reviewed_date"
      ],
      "calendar_freshness": {
        "field": "reviewed_date",
        "stale_days": 365
      }
    }
  ]
